WEBVTT

00:00:00.400 --> 00:00:05.740
<i>Everyone is searching for a new world</i>

00:00:05.740 --> 00:00:11.840
<i>to attain that overflowing dream.</i>

00:00:11.840 --> 00:00:17.420
<i>They all jump over the horizon,</i>

00:00:17.420 --> 00:00:26.190
<i>regardless of what lies beyond.</i>

00:00:29.030 --> 00:00:33.930
<i>We've run,</i>

00:00:33.930 --> 00:00:36.400
<i>we've dived into hope,</i>

00:00:36.400 --> 00:00:39.270
<i>and forgotten only courage.</i>

00:00:39.270 --> 00:00:44.010
<i>And we've been swept away by the crowd</i>

00:00:44.010 --> 00:00:48.670
<i>only to lose something dear to us.</i>

00:00:51.980 --> 00:00:54.350
<i>I smile with a twisted face,</i>

00:00:54.350 --> 00:01:01.020
<i>and it was the best smile I could put on.</i>

00:01:02.290 --> 00:01:04.400
<i>The inside of my mask overflowed with tears</i>

00:01:04.400 --> 00:01:12.040
<i>so I covered my wet mask
with yet another mask.</i>

00:01:12.040 --> 00:01:16.940
<i>I continue to walk through
the flat battleground,</i>

00:01:16.940 --> 00:01:22.180
<i>and I struggle, unable to warp.</i>

00:01:22.180 --> 00:01:32.290
<i>The dream waits quietly on a cape far away.</i>

00:01:32.290 --> 00:01:37.030
<i>Even if I fumble around clumsily,</i>

00:01:37.030 --> 00:01:41.760
<i>I'm sure I'll still be
able to make it there.</i>

00:01:48.670 --> 00:01:52.840
Rio's way too reckless.

00:01:52.840 --> 00:01:57.970
She put her life at risk just to
escape Little Narumi's snare net!

00:01:57.970 --> 00:02:02.150
Rio didn't walk the tightrope
of death to escape.

00:02:02.150 --> 00:02:03.750
Quite the opposite.

00:02:03.750 --> 00:02:07.820
She took a risk to defeat
Little Narumi head on.

00:02:07.820 --> 00:02:11.220
Everything so far has been a
preliminary move toward victory.

00:02:13.690 --> 00:02:15.930
The true match is yet to begin!

00:02:15.930 --> 00:02:20.450
"The Non-Believer's Choice"

00:02:21.830 --> 00:02:24.630
From Rutherford.

00:02:24.630 --> 00:02:26.900
<i>Eyes-kun is so nice!</i>

00:02:31.310 --> 00:02:33.510
So yummy!

00:02:33.510 --> 00:02:37.410
Rio, how do you plan to
defeat Little Narumi now?

00:02:39.080 --> 00:02:41.450
For now, there's something I need.

00:02:41.450 --> 00:02:43.150
Can I ask you for help?

00:02:47.060 --> 00:02:49.290
<i>This is it, Narumi-san!</i>

00:02:49.290 --> 00:02:50.320
Yeah.

00:02:57.030 --> 00:03:00.040
Thank you, you're too kind!

00:03:00.040 --> 00:03:02.610
We're not entirely uninvolved, you see.

00:03:02.610 --> 00:03:04.310
You seem to be recovering well.

00:03:04.310 --> 00:03:06.900
Yeah, I'm recovering great!

00:03:08.110 --> 00:03:10.450
That stuffed animal was a failure.

00:03:10.450 --> 00:03:12.120
Huh?

00:03:12.120 --> 00:03:14.620
We tracked down the store
you bought it from.

00:03:14.620 --> 00:03:18.290
You probably assumed it impossible
to determine where you obtained it

00:03:18.290 --> 00:03:22.290
since the stuffed animal would be
nothing but shreds after it exploded.

00:03:22.290 --> 00:03:25.830
So you didn't bother to choose
a store far from the school

00:03:25.830 --> 00:03:28.530
or even to disguise it.

00:03:28.530 --> 00:03:30.100
You failed.

00:03:30.100 --> 00:03:33.300
A store clerk remembered you
buying that stuffed animal

00:03:33.300 --> 00:03:34.970
the day before the incident.

00:03:34.970 --> 00:03:38.040
Huh? What are you talking about?

00:03:38.040 --> 00:03:42.050
The store's security
camera caught you on tape.

00:03:42.050 --> 00:03:46.150
My information network is
powerful even outside the school!

00:03:46.150 --> 00:03:48.050
Please accept my sympathy.

00:03:51.390 --> 00:03:54.860
<i>Truthfully, the clerk's
testimony wasn't definitive</i>

00:03:54.860 --> 00:03:58.430
<i>and there was no security camera.</i>

00:03:58.430 --> 00:04:02.370
<i>This was all a bluff to
make Rio-san give up.</i>

00:04:02.370 --> 00:04:05.200
<i>It would be rather
embarrassing if she evaded it.</i>

00:04:08.940 --> 00:04:11.700
I won't let you get away, Blade Child!

00:04:14.010 --> 00:04:17.280
<i>Well played, younger
brother of Kiyotaka-sama.</i>

00:04:17.280 --> 00:04:20.410
I'm impressed you could tell I
was one of the Blade Children.

00:04:23.790 --> 00:04:27.760
But if we keep matching our wits like this,

00:04:27.760 --> 00:04:30.760
I don't think we'll ever
reach a conclusion...

00:04:30.760 --> 00:04:32.520
<i>Kosuke-kun!</i>

00:04:33.830 --> 00:04:36.100
Yo, long time no see!

00:04:36.100 --> 00:04:37.330
Asazuki?!

00:04:39.070 --> 00:04:41.640
This is one messed-up situation.

00:04:41.640 --> 00:04:44.210
You sure you can do this?

00:04:44.210 --> 00:04:47.510
Don't worry. I had an inkling
it would come to this.

00:04:47.510 --> 00:04:50.250
If I can't make it through this,

00:04:50.250 --> 00:04:52.510
there's no way I could ever beat fate.

00:04:53.920 --> 00:04:59.120
Now then, Little Brother, let us
begin our non-rigged last game...

00:04:59.120 --> 00:05:00.680
And then end this...

00:05:13.600 --> 00:05:17.370
<i>Access denied to information
about Kiyotaka-san?</i>

00:05:17.370 --> 00:05:18.270
<i>Why?</i>

00:05:18.270 --> 00:05:21.180
<i>I have the appropriate section's password.</i>

00:05:21.180 --> 00:05:24.510
<i>Do I need permission from even higher up?</i>

00:05:24.510 --> 00:05:26.150
<i>It's not just Kiyotaka-san.</i>

00:05:26.150 --> 00:05:28.950
<i>Imazato, Sonobe, Adachi...</i>

00:05:28.950 --> 00:05:32.690
<i>Whenever I try to check into
their pasts I get cut short!</i>

00:05:32.690 --> 00:05:34.760
<i>They all have something...</i>

00:05:34.760 --> 00:05:36.630
<i>Something in common...</i>

00:05:36.630 --> 00:05:37.790
<i>Narumi-kun.</i>

00:05:41.960 --> 00:05:43.730
Senior Superintendent Kanzaka...

00:05:44.630 --> 00:05:46.070
The match is simple,

00:05:46.070 --> 00:05:48.300
and it will conclude this once and for all.

00:05:50.110 --> 00:05:52.710
One is ordinary sugar.

00:05:52.710 --> 00:05:56.110
The other...is strychnine.

00:05:56.110 --> 00:05:57.510
A poison.

00:05:57.510 --> 00:06:00.410
It kills you by causing respiratory
paralysis and circulatory collapse.

00:06:03.120 --> 00:06:05.190
It's extremely bitter,

00:06:05.190 --> 00:06:07.020
and sensitive tongues can still taste it

00:06:07.020 --> 00:06:10.260
even when it's 400,000 times
more diluted than this.

00:06:10.260 --> 00:06:12.930
This is about twice the lethal dosage.

00:06:12.930 --> 00:06:15.990
Even I don't know which is which.

00:06:16.930 --> 00:06:20.940
We'll each choose a cup and then
drink the water down when I say.

00:06:20.940 --> 00:06:23.370
Choose the poison, and you can say goodbye.

00:06:23.370 --> 00:06:25.010
The risk is the same for both of us.

00:06:25.010 --> 00:06:28.310
Which one of us will Death drag away?

00:06:29.480 --> 00:06:31.280
Go ahead and choose first.

00:06:31.280 --> 00:06:33.880
I don't mind having the remaining one.

00:06:33.880 --> 00:06:36.350
That way it wouldn't matter

00:06:36.350 --> 00:06:38.180
even if I did know which one was poisoned.

00:06:40.060 --> 00:06:43.130
Who would ever accept
such a stupid match?!

00:06:43.130 --> 00:06:46.900
Even if we don't bet our lives,
the law will still judge you!

00:06:46.900 --> 00:06:48.660
<i>Can it, though?</i>

00:06:48.660 --> 00:06:50.900
The proof you say you have...

00:06:50.900 --> 00:06:52.660
I get the feeling it's a bluff.

00:06:54.200 --> 00:06:55.910
Did I guess right?

00:06:55.910 --> 00:06:58.310
Why do you insist on this kind of match?

00:06:58.310 --> 00:07:01.480
You could kill me much more
easily if I'm in your way!

00:07:01.480 --> 00:07:04.980
<i>Killing you would be easy.</i>

00:07:04.980 --> 00:07:07.820
But something prevents me from doing so.

00:07:07.820 --> 00:07:09.720
<i>A promise to Kiyotaka-sama.</i>

00:07:11.750 --> 00:07:13.690
<i>A promise to my brother?!</i>

00:07:14.490 --> 00:07:18.150
<i>What do these guys have to
do with my brother?!</i>

00:07:19.830 --> 00:07:21.930
What's the matter?

00:07:21.930 --> 00:07:25.100
<i>Calm down; don't let your
thinking slacken!</i>

00:07:25.100 --> 00:07:28.130
<i>Figure out what she's thinking
and initiate your logic!</i>

00:07:30.610 --> 00:07:33.440
Oh, just so you know, I
haven't done anything cowardly

00:07:33.440 --> 00:07:38.410
like poison both of them so we'll both die.

00:07:38.410 --> 00:07:40.950
Can I believe that?!

00:07:40.950 --> 00:07:44.150
Then shall I drink first?

00:07:44.150 --> 00:07:46.490
If I die, you win.

00:07:46.490 --> 00:07:49.890
If I don't die you can do
whatever you want afterward.

00:07:49.890 --> 00:07:53.430
I won't insist that you
drink the remaining water.

00:07:53.430 --> 00:07:57.630
If you're the type to run away then
there's nothing to be afraid of.

00:07:57.630 --> 00:07:58.970
I'd die if I drank it!

00:07:58.970 --> 00:08:01.500
Only a fool wouldn't run away from that!

00:08:01.500 --> 00:08:03.240
I'd drink it.

00:08:03.240 --> 00:08:05.840
There's no absolute
guarantee that I would die.

00:08:05.840 --> 00:08:08.580
This is twice the lethal dosage
of strychnine we're talking about!

00:08:08.580 --> 00:08:10.710
The chance of surviving
would be virtually zero.

00:08:10.710 --> 00:08:11.910
You'd die instantly!

00:08:11.910 --> 00:08:13.080
I know.

00:08:13.080 --> 00:08:17.250
But being scared and running
away is the same as death.

00:08:18.990 --> 00:08:20.990
A terrible fate will simply snatch away

00:08:20.990 --> 00:08:23.590
that which you desire and hold dear

00:08:23.590 --> 00:08:26.200
and slay your spirit and mind.

00:08:26.200 --> 00:08:27.500
<i>Yes!</i>

00:08:27.500 --> 00:08:30.600
<i>As if Kiyotaka-san took
everything away from you</i>

00:08:30.600 --> 00:08:33.230
<i>and you can only live
with your head down...</i>

00:08:34.340 --> 00:08:36.510
In which case, I won't run away.

00:08:36.510 --> 00:08:40.440
I will go forward to protect what
I hold dear and to change my fate.

00:08:40.440 --> 00:08:44.110
Even if that involves
risking my own life...

00:08:47.120 --> 00:08:49.990
<i>Well? If you can't overcome this,</i>

00:08:49.990 --> 00:08:53.990
then fate will kill you too someday.

00:08:53.990 --> 00:08:56.460
I don't care about fate...

00:08:56.460 --> 00:09:00.050
But it seems I have to defeat you here.

00:09:02.370 --> 00:09:04.600
I accept your challenge.

00:09:08.440 --> 00:09:10.410
Missing persons investigations
are under the jurisdiction

00:09:10.410 --> 00:09:12.440
of the Public Safety Division.

00:09:12.440 --> 00:09:15.780
Detectives like you are not
to get involved with them.

00:09:15.780 --> 00:09:21.120
Basically you're telling me not to
investigate former inspector Narumi?

00:09:21.120 --> 00:09:23.990
I feel bad for the loss of your husband.

00:09:23.990 --> 00:09:27.590
I'm not doing this because
of my personal feelings.

00:09:27.590 --> 00:09:30.930
I need information about him

00:09:30.930 --> 00:09:32.860
to shed light on a series of murders.

00:09:33.600 --> 00:09:35.770
You're an excellent detective.

00:09:35.770 --> 00:09:38.100
I wouldn't want to tarnish your career.

00:09:38.100 --> 00:09:39.270
But!

00:09:39.270 --> 00:09:40.570
Understand?

00:09:44.470 --> 00:09:48.610
Your strategies and tactics won't
be of use now, Little Brother.

00:09:48.610 --> 00:09:51.880
What you need now is the
ability to believe in yourself.

00:09:51.880 --> 00:09:55.250
The conviction that you won't
lose will decide this match.

00:09:59.420 --> 00:10:01.520
Well, here goes...

00:10:01.860 --> 00:10:02.690
Wait!

00:10:03.990 --> 00:10:07.130
Don't assume your little
act will work forever.

00:10:07.130 --> 00:10:10.900
The one who devises strategies
will always be the victor!

00:10:10.900 --> 00:10:13.840
Not the ability to believe or whatever.

00:10:13.840 --> 00:10:15.770
You're really something.

00:10:15.770 --> 00:10:17.740
You're a lot smarter than you look,

00:10:17.740 --> 00:10:19.510
<i>and you have guts.</i>

00:10:19.510 --> 00:10:22.910
To be honest, I was taken aback.

00:10:22.910 --> 00:10:26.020
I wasn't sure anymore that I could
read the psychology of a stupid girl

00:10:26.020 --> 00:10:29.850
who blew her own chest up
to evade the lack of a rib.

00:10:29.850 --> 00:10:32.590
You promptly realized this about me

00:10:32.590 --> 00:10:35.520
and switched from escape to
attack without hesitation.

00:10:35.520 --> 00:10:37.030
The attack being a challenge

00:10:37.030 --> 00:10:40.480
that would make me feel a
definitive sense of defeat.

00:10:41.260 --> 00:10:43.470
Would you seriously propose a match

00:10:43.470 --> 00:10:47.000
that had a 50% chance
of you dying instantly?

00:10:47.000 --> 00:10:50.540
I wouldn't put it past you.

00:10:50.540 --> 00:10:55.180
You did risk your life and knowingly
blow up your chest after all...

00:10:55.180 --> 00:10:58.280
But back then, a snare
net was closing in on you

00:10:58.280 --> 00:11:01.280
and your only choice was to
walk the tightrope of death.

00:11:01.280 --> 00:11:03.150
But how about now?

00:11:03.150 --> 00:11:05.420
You're the one with the
overwhelming advantage.

00:11:05.420 --> 00:11:07.360
My bluff has been called,

00:11:07.360 --> 00:11:10.160
and now I'm out of pieces
to corner you with.

00:11:10.160 --> 00:11:14.300
So why do you find it necessary
to bet your life again?

00:11:14.300 --> 00:11:17.130
Thinking the following would
be the most natural...

00:11:17.130 --> 00:11:21.140
This match is set up to ensure
you a 100% chance of winning.

00:11:21.140 --> 00:11:25.110
But you were the one who
chose the cup first.

00:11:25.110 --> 00:11:27.910
Was there room for me to
set anything like that up?

00:11:27.910 --> 00:11:29.610
More than enough.

00:11:29.610 --> 00:11:32.250
You tried to drink the water first.

00:11:32.250 --> 00:11:33.980
If you didn't die,

00:11:33.980 --> 00:11:37.750
then by process of elimination
my cup would have the poison.

00:11:37.750 --> 00:11:42.390
Would anyone actually drink water
they were told was poisoned?

00:11:42.390 --> 00:11:45.590
Yes. There was never any poison.

00:11:45.590 --> 00:11:47.930
Both powders were sugar.

00:11:47.930 --> 00:11:51.000
You made the preliminary
move of blowing yourself up.

00:11:51.000 --> 00:11:54.500
You've made me believe that
you'll risk your life easily.

00:11:54.500 --> 00:11:57.870
So all you need to is drink
the water and you'll win.

00:11:57.870 --> 00:12:00.880
My only option is to be afraid
of the poison that isn't there

00:12:00.880 --> 00:12:02.280
and admit defeat.

00:12:02.280 --> 00:12:03.780
And then it'll be over.

00:12:03.780 --> 00:12:05.950
I don't need to be told that
being afraid and running away

00:12:05.950 --> 00:12:10.290
is no different than dying...

00:12:10.290 --> 00:12:13.960
You did make one miscalculation
on the way, though...

00:12:13.960 --> 00:12:16.130
If someone died of poisoning here,

00:12:16.130 --> 00:12:19.130
it would be too hard to deal
with the resulting body.

00:12:19.130 --> 00:12:21.560
The police would know,
even if you didn't mess up.

00:12:21.560 --> 00:12:24.230
I doubt you'd do anything that risky.

00:12:25.130 --> 00:12:28.830
Both cups contain sugar water!

00:12:37.750 --> 00:12:39.520
<i>Narumi-san!</i>

00:12:39.520 --> 00:12:40.750
<i>Impossible!</i>

00:12:40.750 --> 00:12:43.150
<i>This tongue-piercing bitterness...</i>

00:12:43.150 --> 00:12:44.750
<i>Strychnine!</i>

00:12:44.750 --> 00:12:46.490
Just what I'd expect from you.

00:12:46.490 --> 00:12:47.990
Even though you talked big,

00:12:47.990 --> 00:12:52.190
you could barely raise the cup to your
lips without being extra cautious.

00:12:52.190 --> 00:12:54.860
There's not nearly enough
for a lethal dose.

00:12:54.860 --> 00:12:57.630
You can't change your fate like that.

00:13:02.100 --> 00:13:05.470
I told you it wasn't rigged...

00:13:05.470 --> 00:13:08.470
<i>She really did bet her life on this!</i>

00:13:10.950 --> 00:13:12.780
<i>Just as Rio thought.</i>

00:13:12.780 --> 00:13:16.390
<i>The ability to believe in
one's self decided everything.</i>

00:13:16.390 --> 00:13:18.950
<i>Little Narumi's reasoning was correct.</i>

00:13:18.950 --> 00:13:22.020
<i>Neither of them contained poison.</i>

00:13:22.020 --> 00:13:25.630
<i>That was extremely bitter
cold medicine in his cup.</i>

00:13:25.630 --> 00:13:27.730
<i>But Rio busted herself up</i>

00:13:27.730 --> 00:13:31.720
<i>and convinced him she's a girl
who would bet her life easily.</i>

00:13:33.100 --> 00:13:38.040
<i>Plus it was announced that the
poison was really bitter strychnine.</i>

00:13:38.040 --> 00:13:39.810
<i>If he sensed even a little bit of bitterness</i>

00:13:39.810 --> 00:13:42.080
<i>he couldn't have drunken any more.</i>

00:13:42.080 --> 00:13:44.910
<i>Unless he really believed in himself.</i>

00:13:44.910 --> 00:13:49.750
<i>In the very end, he yielded
to his own weakness.</i>

00:13:50.820 --> 00:13:53.720
<i>He was supposed to believe in his reasoning</i>

00:13:53.720 --> 00:13:55.820
<i>and drink all the water.</i>

00:13:55.820 --> 00:13:59.850
<i>You can't stand up to destiny
unless you believe in yourself.</i>

00:14:02.260 --> 00:14:03.630
Wait!

00:14:04.600 --> 00:14:08.260
<i>I refuse to believe Narumi-san's
reasoning was wrong!</i>

00:14:09.670 --> 00:14:11.270
The results are already in.

00:14:11.270 --> 00:14:13.880
<i>His reasoning was wrong.</i>

00:14:13.880 --> 00:14:16.780
<i>No! I believe in Narumi-san!</i>

00:14:17.610 --> 00:14:20.310
There's no poison in this cup!

00:14:29.730 --> 00:14:32.960
See, it was just really bitter water.

00:14:37.130 --> 00:14:39.460
This hasn't been settled yet!

00:14:50.250 --> 00:14:52.510
<i>Narumi-san hasn't lost to you.</i>

00:14:52.510 --> 00:14:55.820
So let's have one more match!

00:14:55.820 --> 00:14:58.750
I'll admit, I did use a trick to win...

00:14:58.750 --> 00:15:01.860
<i>But he is the one who lost.</i>

00:15:01.860 --> 00:15:05.590
And he, himself,
should know that very well.

00:15:05.590 --> 00:15:09.770
He admitted defeat by being
unable to verify my trick.

00:15:09.770 --> 00:15:14.400
Standing right there is a cowardly
loser unable to believe in himself.

00:15:14.400 --> 00:15:16.270
Please don't act so full of yourself!

00:15:16.270 --> 00:15:19.540
<i>Narumi-san had a sword to defeat you.</i>

00:15:19.540 --> 00:15:22.040
All you did was manage to dodge it...

00:15:22.040 --> 00:15:25.850
You couldn't really kill him!

00:15:25.850 --> 00:15:28.880
Why didn't you use real poison?

00:15:28.880 --> 00:15:31.790
Why did you rely on a safe trick

00:15:31.790 --> 00:15:34.190
and rig the match so nobody would die?

00:15:34.890 --> 00:15:36.560
<i>If you wanted to defeat Narumi-san,</i>

00:15:36.560 --> 00:15:41.030
you could have put faith in your
luck and truly risked your life,

00:15:41.030 --> 00:15:43.300
but all you did was trick him instead!

00:15:43.300 --> 00:15:46.800
<i>You knew you would lose to Narumi-san</i>

00:15:46.800 --> 00:15:49.810
in an un-rigged match!

00:15:49.810 --> 00:15:52.670
You knew you would be the
one to choose the poison!

00:15:52.670 --> 00:15:55.580
<i>You feared Narumi-san's ability.</i>

00:15:55.580 --> 00:15:57.080
You weren't afraid of the bomb,

00:15:57.080 --> 00:15:59.380
<i>but you were afraid of Narumi-san!</i>

00:15:59.380 --> 00:16:01.920
<i>You were the one who ran away first!</i>

00:16:01.920 --> 00:16:04.390
You can't stick your chest
out and be triumphant!

00:16:05.390 --> 00:16:07.620
You're a very frightening person...

00:16:08.360 --> 00:16:11.090
<i>You pierced the part that
hurts me the most...</i>

00:16:12.330 --> 00:16:15.600
But today's not your lucky day.

00:16:15.600 --> 00:16:19.330
<i>Kiyotaka-sama limited me in regards
to the treatment of Little Narumi,</i>

00:16:19.330 --> 00:16:24.410
but he doesn't care what
I do to anybody else.

00:16:24.410 --> 00:16:26.410
If you're going to get in my way,

00:16:26.410 --> 00:16:28.680
then I won't count out removing you.

00:16:28.680 --> 00:16:30.880
You're planning to kill me too?

00:16:30.880 --> 00:16:33.120
<i>Just like Imazato-sensei?</i>

00:16:33.120 --> 00:16:36.190
Yes, murder is easy.

00:16:36.190 --> 00:16:40.190
And there's nothing to fear
if you kill all your enemies.

00:16:40.190 --> 00:16:44.290
<i>I killed Imazato-sensei easily, too.</i>

00:16:44.290 --> 00:16:46.660
I've been waiting for you to say that!

00:16:46.660 --> 00:16:50.260
I just recorded everything you've said!

00:16:52.330 --> 00:16:54.900
<i>You admitted to killing Imazato-sensei.</i>

00:16:54.900 --> 00:16:58.540
Plus you threatened to kill me.

00:16:58.540 --> 00:17:01.910
These are pretty strong
pieces of evidence, you know!

00:17:02.640 --> 00:17:05.910
I've been recording since
I entered the room,

00:17:05.910 --> 00:17:10.450
but I had a hard time getting
you to say the definitive lines.

00:17:10.450 --> 00:17:12.920
You were probably being cautious,

00:17:12.920 --> 00:17:15.960
but in the very end,
you let your guard down!

00:17:15.960 --> 00:17:20.560
<i>Now I have a foothold to
get you arrested, Rio-san!</i>

00:17:20.560 --> 00:17:22.930
You're good!

00:17:22.930 --> 00:17:26.500
You save the trump card until
the very end for a reason!

00:17:26.500 --> 00:17:29.870
<i>Hiyono-san. What is it you want?</i>

00:17:29.870 --> 00:17:33.740
I assume you don't want something as
simple as giving me to the police.

00:17:33.740 --> 00:17:35.940
That's right. I have one wish.

00:17:35.940 --> 00:17:38.340
<i>A rematch between you and Narumi-san!</i>

00:17:39.280 --> 00:17:42.680
What the hell are you thinking?!

00:17:42.680 --> 00:17:46.050
About you! Don't you like that idea?

00:17:57.700 --> 00:17:58.690
<i>Narumi-san!</i>

00:18:02.840 --> 00:18:04.910
Why, you little!

00:18:04.910 --> 00:18:06.610
You go too far, girl!

00:18:06.610 --> 00:18:09.810
Oh? But this is nothing!

00:18:09.810 --> 00:18:12.250
<i>Narumi-san, go!</i>

00:18:12.250 --> 00:18:13.380
Hurry!

00:18:13.380 --> 00:18:14.970
Oh, no you don't!

00:18:16.650 --> 00:18:18.090
Hand over the tape!

00:18:18.090 --> 00:18:21.590
Unless you wanna see this
girl fall from here!

00:18:21.590 --> 00:18:25.590
<i>Narumi-san! I'm safe as
long as you have that tape!</i>

00:18:25.590 --> 00:18:29.400
As long as you have that,
there's no point in killing me!

00:18:29.400 --> 00:18:31.600
Besides, they're not the
kind of people who would want

00:18:31.600 --> 00:18:34.500
a conclusion that ends in
brute force like this!

00:18:34.500 --> 00:18:36.270
<i>Go, Narumi-san!</i>

00:18:36.270 --> 00:18:39.010
And then face off against
them one more time!

00:18:39.010 --> 00:18:41.070
Believe in your strength!

00:18:49.620 --> 00:18:50.750
Dammit!

00:18:50.750 --> 00:18:55.120
Oh well, I guess we should just
hold on to her for a while...

00:18:55.890 --> 00:18:59.050
<i>Kosuke-kun, you might
want to let go of her...</i>

00:19:05.070 --> 00:19:08.440
This special stun gun has a max
voltage of 1 million volts -

00:19:08.440 --> 00:19:10.310
enough to knock even a bear to the ground!

00:19:10.310 --> 00:19:12.710
You shouldn't carry dangerous
stuff like that around!

00:19:12.710 --> 00:19:15.040
Oh, but what's the point of even having it

00:19:15.040 --> 00:19:17.580
if I can't carry it
around to protect myself?

00:19:17.580 --> 00:19:21.980
So you could've run away
if you had wanted to?

00:19:21.980 --> 00:19:24.040
You could say that!

00:19:24.920 --> 00:19:27.390
Why didn't you run away?

00:19:27.390 --> 00:19:32.160
Being a hostage would make
Narumi-san more spirited.

00:19:32.160 --> 00:19:33.330
What?

00:19:33.330 --> 00:19:36.670
<i>You must really want me and
Kiyotaka-sama's little brother</i>

00:19:36.670 --> 00:19:38.830
to have a rematch, huh?

00:19:38.830 --> 00:19:44.210
But letting him run away
wasn't the correct choice.

00:19:44.210 --> 00:19:46.110
Even though a comeback
is nearly impossible,

00:19:46.110 --> 00:19:49.750
he ran away and left the girl behind.

00:19:49.750 --> 00:19:51.450
I think he's in for a real mental shock

00:19:51.450 --> 00:19:54.880
when he thinks about what he's done...

00:19:54.880 --> 00:19:57.250
He's been basically finished off.

00:19:58.090 --> 00:20:02.220
When you fall it's best to fall
straight to the very bottom!

00:20:02.220 --> 00:20:04.890
The farther that boys crawl back up,

00:20:04.890 --> 00:20:08.560
the stronger and greater they become!

00:20:13.440 --> 00:20:15.740
Things have become quite complicated.

00:20:15.740 --> 00:20:17.510
Yeah, I suppose.

00:20:17.510 --> 00:20:20.610
So where's the Hiyono girl?

00:20:20.610 --> 00:20:23.010
She's under confinement for now.

00:20:25.250 --> 00:20:27.580
So Little Narumi was let loose

00:20:27.580 --> 00:20:30.550
and now wanders the field, ever the loser...

00:20:31.250 --> 00:20:33.460
<i>Kiyotaka said it best...</i>

00:20:33.460 --> 00:20:35.120
<i>The strength to get up after a defeat</i>

00:20:35.120 --> 00:20:39.360
<i>is more admirable than the
strength to never lose.</i>

00:20:43.830 --> 00:20:47.340
<i>This will ensure the tape's safety...</i>

00:20:47.340 --> 00:20:48.560
<i>But...</i>

00:20:50.440 --> 00:20:52.540
<i>I ran away...</i>

00:20:52.540 --> 00:20:54.630
<i>I left her behind!</i>

00:20:56.680 --> 00:20:59.310
<i>My brother wouldn't have hesitated...</i>

00:20:59.310 --> 00:21:04.080
<i>My brother would have believed
in himself and never hesitated!</i>

00:21:06.210 --> 00:21:11.920
<i>A sweet scent washes into my throat</i>

00:21:11.920 --> 00:21:18.620
<i>and my feelings continuously overflow...</i>

00:21:30.740 --> 00:21:36.780
<i>Don't look at me with that same gaze</i>

00:21:36.780 --> 00:21:42.420
<i>that's like you're following a soccer ball.</i>

00:21:42.420 --> 00:21:48.320
<i>I've already grown used to
my third year at the office,</i>

00:21:48.320 --> 00:21:54.900
<i>but did I lose something instead?</i>

00:21:54.900 --> 00:22:00.630
<i>Those days long ago when we
would talk about anything...</i>

00:22:00.630 --> 00:22:05.840
<i>We're finally old enough now</i>

00:22:05.840 --> 00:22:11.680
<i>to have those slightly awkward
discussions about love.</i>

00:22:11.680 --> 00:22:23.290
<i>A single day seems so long,
but a whole year ends so quickly.</i>

00:22:23.290 --> 00:22:29.060
<i>A whole year seems so short,</i>

00:22:29.060 --> 00:22:35.370
<i>but how well will I be able
to live the rest of my life?</i>

00:22:39.760 --> 00:22:41.960
Time for Hiyono's Useful News Report!

00:22:43.660 --> 00:22:47.100
When we fall, let's fall straight
to the very, very bottom!

00:22:47.100 --> 00:22:51.100
All we have to do after
that is crawl back up!

00:22:51.100 --> 00:22:53.510
<i>Next episode's highlight is when
Narumi-san goes bungee jumping</i>

00:22:53.510 --> 00:22:56.110
after regaining his
determination under a waterfall!

00:22:56.110 --> 00:22:58.280
On the next Spiral: Bond of Reasoning...

00:22:58.280 --> 00:22:59.680
The Day of Losers

00:22:59.680 --> 00:23:04.220
Boys grow stronger and greater
the farther they have to crawl up!

00:23:04.220 --> 00:23:06.480
That's all for today's Hiyono's Playhouse!
